## 14) CURSOR / AI ENFORCEMENT RULES

**AI MUST:**

- Avoid `any`
- Avoid `extends`
- Prefer composition
- Use utility types (Pick, Omit, Partial, ReturnType, etc.) when deriving from existing types
- Explicitly type everything
- Mark uncertainty clearly

**AI MUST NOT:**

- Silence TypeScript
- Cast away errors
- Introduce inheritance chains
- Add complex types without justification
- Chain many utility types; prefer one or two steps and named aliases

